# One column of the `properties` sweep: every `ui/style` property that paints
# something, at three to five values each, over a `button`, whose styles land
# on the button itself.
#
# Six pictures, one per family, each a labelled grid — the property down the
# page, its values across it. The values are the ends of the range and a middle,
# and they name their unit where the unit changes the answer: pixels, rems, a
# percentage of the containing box.
#
# Resting state only. No style here sits inside an `On`, so the state the
# snapshot is taken in contributes nothing; `sweep_states_*` is where a state
# is the subject. Nor is any property here a layout one — `Layout`, the
# alignments, `Grow`, `Shrink`, `Span`, `Pin` and `Position` belong to
# `sweep_layout_*`, and tokens and breakpoints to `sweep_themes_*`.
#
# The lifecycle is `every_shape_and_state_is_painted`'s: every golden compares,
# a renamed snapshot is reported as missing rather than as a difference,
# `--update` records it, the run after that compares against what it wrote, and
# an edit that widens one cell fails the comparison. Only the first run paints
# the whole suite; the four after it are `--filter`ed to the one picture they
# are about, because painting six 800 by 600 pages five times over is four
# fifths of what this case would cost the bar.
#
# **Four of these pictures are pinned as painted rather than as right**, and each
# is a filed bug. Re-record the goldens as each closes.
#
#   * #86 — a `Width` or a `Height` is a border box, so the padding sits inside
#     it. Visible wherever the `size` picture puts a length against the base's
#     two pixels of padding.
#   * #87 — a translucent `Foreground`, and any fractional `Opacity`, paint the
#     glyphs fully opaque. The `surface` picture's third `Foreground` cell and
#     its `Opacity` band.
#   * #78 — `Truncate` paints every line, so all four cells of the `runs`
#     picture's last band are one picture.
#   * #81 — `TextWrap(.Balance)` paints exactly as `.Wrap` does.
#
# Three bands are the same picture across their values on purpose, and each says
# something. `FontFamily`: every family resolves to the one bundled face, which
# is what keeps a snapshot the same bytes on two hosts. A `Gap` or a
# `ListMarker` on a primitive whose styled element holds one child or none has
# nothing to space or to mark, which is what the DOM does with it too. And
# `Scroll`'s three axes are one picture because CSS computes `visible` to `auto`
# on the other axis, so any of them clips both ways.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs.

doc: "every ui/style property that paints, at three to five values each, over a `button`, whose styles land on the button itself, as 6 pictures with the whole record-and-fail lifecycle over them"

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "pass.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/button-surface.diff.png"  exists: false }

# A snapshot nobody has recorded yet is reported as missing, with the command
# that records one, rather than as a difference against nothing.
edit {
  file: "lib/sweep/test/pictures.buri"
  replace: "\"button-surface\""
  with: "\"never-recorded\""
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=surface"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "missing.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: false }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--update", "--force", "--filter=surface"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "recorded.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/never-recorded.png"  exists: true }

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=surface"]
  exit: 0
  golden: "again.txt"
}

# The negative twin: four pixels on one cell of the `size` picture, which is the
# smallest edit that has to fail.
edit {
  file: "lib/sweep/scenes.buri"
  replace: ".Width(.Px(40))"
  with: ".Width(.Px(44))"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/sweep", "--force", "--filter=sizing"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "changed.txt"
}

path { path: "lib/sweep/test/__snapshots__/button-size.diff.png"  exists: true }
